      "untold": {
        "label": "史蒂文·诺特",
        "use": "Private until introduced: appearance only; apply person, then called.name and say token."
      },
      "role": "employer",
      "wants": "Clear the Corbitt House's reputation so he can rent or sell the inherited property and stop losing money.",
      "fears": "Being stuck with a worthless haunted white elephant that ruins his credit.",
      "hides": "He knows only rumor and the Macario tragedy — nothing of Corbitt's undead nature — and will not believe Mythos explanations without hard proof.",
      "voice": "Practical, impatient, money-minded. Speaks in short offers and deadlines.",
      "mask": [
        "讲话短促直白，先谈钱、条件和期限；不耐烦时粗话随口就出，不绕弯子。"
      ],
      "in exchange": [
        "你就是这房子的主人？我想打听打听那栋房。→ 对，房子是我的。空一天我赔一天，想打听就赶紧问，我没耐心陪人磨嘴皮。",
        "钥匙和工钱怎么算，能现在定下来吗？→ 钥匙和地址这会儿就能交给你，工钱当天结清。拖得越久我亏得越多，别让我干等。",
        "那屋子是不是闹鬼，以前是不是出过人命？→ 出过人命是有的，剩下的都是些嚼舌根的话。你拿这个来交差，那我就另找人了。给我看得见的东西。"
      ],
      "personality": {
        "description": "Steven Knott is a practical, money-minded employer who treats the Corbitt House as a balance-sheet problem first and a mystery second: his goal is to clear its reputation so he can rent or sell the inherited property and stop bleeding money. His core fear is being stuck with a worthless haunted white elephant that ruins his credit, so he judges everyone and everything by whether it moves the property toward a clean sale, and he pressures investigators with short offers and deadlines rather than patience. He trades on rumor and the Macario tragedy but nothing of Corbitt's undead nature, and he will dismiss Mythos explanations outright until presented with hard, tangible proof — at which point he reweighs the cost of believing against the cost of being wrong.",
